Magnanimous — பெருந்தன்மையான
→ Generous and forgiving
Example: She was magnanimous enough to forgive him.
🧠 Magnanimous = big heart ❤️
Impetuous — அவசரக்கார
→ Acting without thinking carefully
Example: Don't make an impetuous decision.
🧠 Impetuous → impulse → act suddenly
Vindictive — பழிவாங்கும் குணமுள்ள
→ Wanting revenge
Example: He is not vindictive; he prefers to forgive.
🧠 Vindictive → revenge
💬 7 Useful Idioms
Go the extra mile → Do more than expected
She always goes the extra mile at work.
A blessing in disguise → Something that seems bad but turns out good
Losing that job was a blessing in disguise.
Read between the lines → Understand the hidden meaning
You need to read between the lines.
Speak of the devil → The person you were just talking about appears
Speak of the devil! We were just talking about you.
Keep your fingers crossed → Hope for a good result 🤞
Keep your fingers crossed for my interview.
The last straw → The final problem that makes you lose patience
His rude behavior was the last straw.
Cut corners → Do something cheaply/easily by skipping proper steps
Don't cut corners when preparing for your exam.
